{
  "name": "showcase",
  "vibe": "An annotated product tour, shot like a guided walkthrough. Near-white paper washed with soft colour blobs and a fine 52px grid; paper planes cross the sky. Real screenshots ride inside real device chrome — a browser window with a URL bar, a phone with a notch — and the film ANNOTATES them the way a product tour does: curved arrows draw themselves toward a feature, numbered callout bubbles pop at the point they name, a highlight box pulses around a region, a cursor travels and clicks, and one screen slowly zooms toward its focal point. Beats cut hard, each one pushed in and out by a slide camera. Authored landscape-first (16:9) as a native GSAP + DOM composition. Best for SaaS, developer tools, dashboards, mobile apps and anything whose story IS its interface — this pack shows the product rather than describing it, and wants real screenshots to do it.",
